- op: discuss  # 8533
  at: '2026-03-03T06:22:04Z'  # 8533
  by: agent  # 8533
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8533
  clock: 9  # 8533
  nonce: '8533'  # 8533
  message: "External bakeoff (March 2026) revealed a feature parity gap in route graph materialization:\n\n- Rails (gitlab): 5,223 route nodes, 1,275 routes_to edges, end-to-end slice traversal ✅\n- Go (grafana): 483 route nodes, 474 routes_to edges ✅\n- Java/JAX-RS (keycloak): 0 route nodes, 0 routes_to edges, despite 1,302 routes in routes.txt ❌\n\nThis is a feature-parity violation: route→handler graph materialization works for Rails and Go but not for Java. The detection stage (annotation recognition) works for all three, but the materialization stage (creating kind=route nodes + routes_to edges) is only implemented for Rails (centralized config/routes.rb) and Go (explicit r.GET() calls). Java's distributed @Path annotation chains aren't synthesized into graph nodes.\n\nNew WI-lodik created for the Java-specific fix. This INV should track this as an open feature parity gap."  # 8533
